WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.310
Salt is sodium chloride:

2
00:00:02.360 --> 00:00:07.410
a giant lattice of positive sodium
ions and negative chloride ions.

3
00:00:07.460 --> 00:00:11.750
Every grain in the salt cellar
is packed with charged particles.

4
00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:15.810
Now wire a single salt crystal
into a circuit with a bulb.

5
00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:18.130
The bulb stays dark.

6
00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:20.630
Salt is made of charged particles.

7
00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:23.970
So why doesn't a salt
crystal conduct electricity?

8
00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:27.510
In this mission, you'll work
out which ions atoms form,

9
00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:31.470
and write the formulae and
names of ionic compounds.

10
00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:33.870
You'll explain the properties
of an ionic lattice,

11
00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:37.990
and compare how strongly
different lattices hold together.

12
00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:42.530
Your mission: explain why solid
salt doesn't conduct electricity.
